From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] wgl: the caller's reference to a new swapchain texture

The DXGI framebuffer's get_resource gave the caller a reference of its own for a texture it had made before, but for
a new one it returned the reference it kept: the window's framebuffer (stw_st) and the DXGI framebuffer each released
a texture referenced once. Whichever released it second touched freed memory - mostly unnoticed, now and then an
access violation in stw_st's release loop while the window was destroyed (0xC000041D, an exception in a window
procedure: dx-test's OpenGL groups, about one run in five on Windows 10; found with dx-test's exception notes,
viogpu_wgl.dll+0x272f). New textures get the caller's reference too.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/targets/wgl/dxgi_framebuffer.cpp b/src/gallium/targets/wgl/dxgi_framebuffer.cpp
index 8b4a853..60d7a5b 100644
--- a/src/gallium/targets/wgl/dxgi_framebuffer.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/targets/wgl/dxgi_framebuffer.cpp
@@ -249,6 +249,9 @@ wgl_dxgi_framebuffer_get_resource(struct stw_winsys_framebuffer *pframebuffer,
    struct pipe_resource *texture =
       fb->screen->resource_from_handle(fb->screen, nullptr, &whandle, 0);
    fb->textures[index] = texture;
+   /* the caller's reference, as for a texture made before (the framebuffer keeps its own: both release theirs) */
+   if (texture)
+      pipe_reference(NULL, &texture->reference);
    return texture;
 }
 
